lisa-addressed:
Human review round 5 (gusfcarvalho, PR #456) — 21 findings, all valid, all fixed.

- [Blocker] Integration build broken: risk_evidence_worker_test_helpers_test.go:49 still assigned
  LeveragedAuthUUID: uuid.New() after the field became *uuid.UUID. FIXED: dropped the field (it is
  optional now and the test never reads it). Verified with `go vet -tags integration`. Also fixed
  the stale SSPLeverageHandler type doc (ssp_leverage.go:158) still claiming subscribe records a
  leveraged-authorization.
- [High] resyncLeverageSatisfaction found links by (downstream_ssp_id, provided_uuid). The unique
  index on that pair is what ENABLES the bug rather than preventing it: exactly one link exists per
  pair, but InheritedControlImplementation has NO unique index, so two by-components in one SSP can
  each hold an inherited row for the same provided-uuid — and resync for B would rewrite A's link
  from B's satisfied set. FIXED: one query keyed on `inherited_uuid IN (this bc's inherited ids)`,
  which disambiguates AND removes the N+1 First() loop. Also added a 409 on a provided-uuid already
  inherited elsewhere in the same SSP (new byComponentIDsForSSP helper walks
  control_implementations -> implemented_requirements -> statements -> by_components; there is no
  SSP id below control_implementations).
- [High] deleteByComponentCascade was TOCTOU: guard counted links against the PRELOADED inherited
  set while the deletes were bulk `by_component_id = ?`, and it took no lock (nor did any of its
  three callers). FIXED: takes lockByComponentSubtreeWrite BEFORE the preload, and deletes are
  scoped to `id IN (checked ids)` so the rows destroyed are exactly the rows guarded — which also
  fixes the orphaned responsible_roles. NOTE for the reviewer: the `len(bc.Inherited) > 0` gate was
  NOT an independent hole (empty IN ? renders as no-match, so linkCount is 0 and the guard passes
  either way) — the missing lock plus fixed-set-vs-bulk-delete is the real defect.
- [High] filter.go:522 resolved controls by `LOWER(id)` alone, ignoring Control's composite PK
  (catalog_id, id). FIXED with resolveCatalogIDForSSPControl: resolve via the SSP's own profiles
  first (authoritative), else fall back to the catalogs defining the control — exactly one resolves,
  more than one is a 400 (errAmbiguousControlCatalog). DESIGN NOTE: a hard 404 when the SSP's
  profiles don't import the control was rejected — resolveCatalogIDForControl's own doc says a
  downstream need not have the leveraged control in its profile, and the existing fixture seeds no
  ssp_profiles, so a hard 404 would break legitimate use. The point is that NO arbitrary choice is
  ever made. The join carries no CAST (per the sqlite/uuid trap; matches
  system_component_suggestions.go's precedent).
- [Medium] filter.go:547 co-ownership count not catalog-scoped. FIXED: + control_catalog_id.
- [Medium] filter.go:623 unwind count missing BOTH control_catalog_id AND control_link_created=true.
  FIXED. The control_link_created half was the damaging one (a non-claiming row stranded the link
  permanently). Regression test added: TestDetachUnwindsLinkDespiteUnowningSibling.
- [Low] filter.go inheritance check ignored link status. DECIDED EXPLICITLY: `status NOT IN
  (revoked, superseded)` — a drifted link still qualifies (subscription exists, being reconciled);
  terminal states do not. Comment states the reasoning.
- [Medium] ByControl unbounded. FIXED: extracted parseExportOfferingPagination, shared with ListAll
  so the two cannot drift; same 100/1000 bounds. Swagger documents limit/offset.
- [Medium] Satisfied create validated inheritability on h.db, outside the tx and before the lock.
  FIXED: inheritableResponsibilities now takes a *gorm.DB and runs inside the tx after the lock;
  400 preserved via errResponsibilityNotInheritable sentinel.
- [Medium] Inherited DELETE took no lock. FIXED: locks on existing.ByComponentId before the count.
- [Medium] By-component PUT zeroed omitted fields (map-form Updates writes every key). FIXED with
  real MERGE semantics — the update map is built from the keys actually present in the raw body
  (read before Bind consumes it). Chose merge over weakening the docs because the swagger claim is
  already published. NOTE: responsible-roles deliberately stays REPLACE — an omitted roles list
  clears them, pinned by the existing TestUpdateByComponentReplacesResponsibleRoles. I had gated it
  too at first; that test correctly caught it as scope creep.
- [Medium] migrator ALTER TABLE ran unconditionally every boot (ACCESS EXCLUSIVE, no lock_timeout
  anywhere). FIXED with the information_schema is_nullable='NO' guard, matching the eight existing
  DO $$ ... IF EXISTS blocks in the same function.
- [Medium] Backfill: unbounded load, unbounded IN-lists (65535 bind ceiling -> fatal at boot),
  un-deduped id lists, one implicit tx per row. FIXED: FindInBatches, local uniqueUUIDs +
  findByIDsInChunks helpers (uniqueUUIDs in handler/oscal is unexported, so unreachable from
  internal/service regardless of cycles), all writes in one db.Transaction.
- [Low] undeterminable counter collapsed 4 causes. FIXED: four named counters, log distinguishes
  corruption (dangling provided-uuid / missing export) from expected legacy (requirement-anchored),
  plus the item ids.
- [Low] Duplicate exports silently dropped. FIXED: exportsByComponent is now a slice map and every
  export is reported; Offered unions across them. Deliberately did NOT add the unique index —
  existing data may violate it and AutoMigrate would fail at boot (same fatal-migration hazard).
- [Medium] Client-supplied UUID collision returned 500. FIXED: reuses the existing isUniqueViolation
  and maps to 409 on both create paths via errDuplicateInheritedUUID / errDuplicateSatisfiedUUID.
- [Low] Stale comment claiming a re-derivation that isn't there. FIXED: comment now says the lock
  serializes concurrent creates. No resync added — creating an inherited row changes what is
  inheritable, not what is satisfied, exactly as the reviewer reasoned.
- [Medium] TestSubscribeReportsReusedRowsAsNotCreated asserted created:TRUE. FIXED: it now makes a
  SECOND subscribe call and asserts Created==false for requirement, statement AND by-component
  (previously asserted nowhere in the repo). The dedup assertions moved to
  TestSubscribeDedupesReportedRowsWithinOneCall.
- [Medium] subtree_lock_invariant_test was a hand-maintained allowlist. FIXED: INVERTED to
  discovery — AST-walks the package for functions calling resyncLeverageSatisfaction or writing
  SSPLeverageLink.Satisfaction, and requires each DISCOVERED writer to take the lock; the known-five
  map is now only a superset assertion against a vacuous walk. callsFunc handles *ast.SelectorExpr.
  VERIFIED BOTH WAYS: fails when the lock is removed from resync, AND fails for a newly added
  unlocked writer (the exact regression the allowlist could not catch). Also added
  subtree_lock_concurrency_integration_test.go (//go:build integration, real Postgres, two
  concurrent goroutines) per the reviewer's request. NOTE: the comment said no *unit* test can
  observe the lock, which is literally true — but the substantive point stood.
- [Low] gofmt-dirty ssp_leverage_drift_test.go. FIXED. Only cedar_test.go remains, pre-existing on
  main as the reviewer noted.
- [Low] Duplicated subscription-ownership guard. FIXED: extracted assertInheritedNotSubscribed,
  called from both the cascade and the sub-resource DELETE.

VERIFICATION: go build ./... clean; go vet -tags integration ./... clean; full unit suite 37/37 ok;
gofmt clean except pre-existing cedar_test.go; swagger regenerated (make swag) so check-diff stays
clean. The new integration suites could NOT be run locally (no Docker daemon available) — they
compile under -tags integration and CI must exercise them.
